<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) (Drosophila melanogaster (third-instar larval wing imaginal disc, 64h-96h AEL))",
        "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) faithfully reproduces Drosophila melanogaster (third-instar larval wing imaginal disc, 64h-96h AEL) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster (third-instar larval wing imaginal disc, 64h-96h AEL) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 85.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-wing-disc-dome-folding-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster (third-instar larval wing imaginal disc, 64h-96h AEL)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element mesh, dorsoventral curvature, PE growth or PE fold mechanics, a measured wing-disc lumen pressure, or an emergent (untethered) fold pattern",
        "reconstructed_in_script: L-BFGS-B 2D sagittal apico-basal bilayer with multiplicative growth stretch, stiff BM tether and local fold remodeling (Pass 2); Pass 3 adds a quasi-1D plane-strain sac: neo-Hookean BM shell tension, shallow-cap Laplace dome deflection, tensioned PE membrane in unilateral contact, lumen pressure closed by prescribed volume (bisection) or imposed, an imposed-pressure sweep, a PE-ablation control, 13 measurements and 10 self-test checks",
        "reported_in_source: McClure & Schubiger (2005): the peripodial epithelium is a thin squamous layer overlying the columnar disc proper (used only for h_PE ~ 3 um; DOI not verified offline)",
        "reported_in_source: Mosaliganti et al. (2019): epithelial lumen pressures of ~100-300 Pa in the zebrafish otic vesicle (order-of-magnitude context only; NOT wing-disc data; DOI not verified offline)",
        "reported_in_source: Sui et al. (2018): differential lateral and basal tension drive H/H vs H/P folding by two distinct mechanisms",
        "reported_in_source: Tozluoglu et al. (2019): planar differential growth rates in the third-instar wing disc, together with the basal ECM, position the H/N, H/H and H/P folds precisely; uniform growth gives unpinned buckling; Collagenase flattens the dome and abolishes folds",
        "transfer_boundary: T_PE = 1 mN/m, h_lumen = 12 um, h_margin = 8 um and T_cell = 0.5 mN/m are order-of-magnitude assumptions with no wing-disc measurement; the self-consistent p = 0.62 Pa and p_half = 372.5 Pa are model predictions with no published value to compare",
        "transfer_boundary: The bilayer 'relaxed' surface is tethered to a hand-built target shape (dome envelope, stage scaling and Gaussian cleft depths fitted to the reference table), so the 64-96 h dome and fold-depth correlations largely reproduce the prescription rather than emerge from g(s)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Polygonal Packing & Furrows" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Shape Index p_0* = 3.813" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py; output: docs/media/wing_disc_dome_folding_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila melanogaster (third-instar larval wing imaginal disc, 64h-96h AEL); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 2af2500d7102510b3e1d9092d6e108c583a8e75540249273bb0089532f4c3517; artifact_sha256: d96fd9da4de81ddd20c5d03b4b0e3e12157621e79cfe3dd7746c18d9ad79ae97; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/drosophila_wing_disc_specimen.jpg=b523296d0ee292e1..., datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/peripodial_lumen_reference.json=972d43d7d4fc991a..., datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/scout_manifest.json=0f2a2d1d54a8d262..., datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/wing_disc_dome_folding_reference.json=c4c99a6cca181df7...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-wing-disc-dome-folding-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Tozluoglu et al. (2019): planar differential growth rates in the third-instar wing disc, together with the basal ECM, position the H/N, H/H and H/P folds precisely; uniform growth gives unpinned buckling; Collagenase flattens the dome and abolishes folds | Sui et al. (2018): differential lateral and basal tension drive H/H vs H/P folding by two distinct mechanisms | McClure & Schubiger (2005): the peripodial epithelium is a thin squamous layer overlying the columnar disc proper (used only for h_PE ~ 3 um; DOI not verified offline) | Mosaliganti et al. (2019): epithelial lumen pressures of ~100-300 Pa in the zebrafish otic vesicle (order-of-magnitude context only; NOT wing-disc data; DOI not verified offline); reconstructed_in_script: L-BFGS-B 2D sagittal apico-basal bilayer with multiplicative growth stretch, stiff BM tether and local fold remodeling (Pass 2); Pass 3 adds a quasi-1D plane-strain sac: neo-Hookean BM shell tension, shallow-cap Laplace dome deflection, tensioned PE membrane in unilateral contact, lumen pressure closed by prescribed volume (bisection) or imposed, an imposed-pressure sweep, a PE-ablation control, 13 measurements and 10 self-test checks; transfer_boundary: The bilayer 'relaxed' surface is tethered to a hand-built target shape (dome envelope, stage scaling and Gaussian cleft depths fitted to the reference table), so the 64-96 h dome and fold-depth correlations largely reproduce the prescription rather than emerge from g(s) | T_PE = 1 mN/m, h_lumen = 12 um, h_margin = 8 um and T_cell = 0.5 mN/m are order-of-magnitude assumptions with no wing-disc measurement; the self-consistent p = 0.62 Pa and p_half = 372.5 Pa are model predictions with no published value to compare; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element mesh, dorsoventral curvature, PE growth or PE fold mechanics, a measured wing-disc lumen pressure, or an emergent (untethered) fold pattern]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2019.09.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-06497-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.4032128>,
