<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the module header (L1-70) maps Laws 1-4 to the Lean theorems by name and lists the DOIs; every new Pass 3 function has a docstring stating the equation, the compartments and that T_PE / h_lumen / h_margin / T_cell are assumptions (L59-65, L143-147, L559-561, L620); the `peripodial_ablation` entry is labelled a prediction (L914, L922); the sweep figure footer states 'quasi-1D plane-strain (residual: no 3D FEM)' (L1488); Law 4 is registered in `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.yaml`. Deductions: the fitted constants 4.2 + 49.8 frac^0.88, 0.861, 0.959, 0.092, 0.557/0.443, 0.623, 15.35/19.95/16.75 and c_finite = 8.395 carry no citation or 'fitted to reference' label (L208, L354-394) (-5); the `self_test` docstring says '8-point ... for Pass 2' (L1755) and the `--self-test` help says '8-check' (L1853) while 10 checks run (-2); Law 3 in Lean (L116-149) proves an ordering of hand-picked integers and Law 4 is likewise integer inequalities, which the header presents as governing mathematics (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L1753–L1755: self_test docstring still says '8-point verification suite for Pass 2' (10 checks run) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L1753-L1755>",
        "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L1853–L1853: --self-test help string says '8-check' (stale) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L1853-L1853>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the Pass 3 sac is a physically coherent reduced model — neo-Hookean BM membrane tension T_DP = mu_BM h_BM (gamma^2 - gamma^-4) + T_cell (L521-534), shallow-cap Laplace response dz = p chord^2 / (16 T_DP) (L536-547), PE membrane energy sum 0.5 T_PE (dz/dx)^2 - p z with unilateral contact z_PE >= z_DP + h_min through L-BFGS-B bounds (L550-590), and a volume-closed lumen pressure by bisection with PE-ablation reducing exactly to the uncoupled DP (L592-742); Law 4 is machine-checked (Lean L168-207) and the Law 2 trough second difference is proven invariant to a uniform load. Deductions: the Pass 2 bilayer (L267-519) builds `z_target` from a hand-tuned dome envelope (L354-368), stage scaling (L371-374) and Gaussian cleft amplitudes with per-condition multipliers 0.861 / 0.959 / 1 + 0.092(...) and `remodel_mult` / `jak_mult` (L383-394) fitted to the reference, and tethers the solution to it with k_tether = 1.0 (L414), so folds are prescribed rather than emergent from g(s) (-9); `c_finite = 8.395` (L208) is calibrated to the 0.0128 um^-1 reference (-3); the lumen is quasi-1D per unit D-V width with no PE growth or fold mechanics and no 3D mesh, which is the v2 item still open (-4); the pressure-mode sweep lets the PE sag > 100 um for p > 10 Pa, so the sweep is a DP-only response, not a sac equilibrium (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L193–L211: compute_bilayer_dome_curvature with c_finite = 8.395 calibrated to the 0.0128 um^-1 reference <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L193-L211>",
        "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L354–L414: Target shape: dome_amp_stage with fitted per-condition multipliers, fold_stage_scale, cleft depths 15.35/19.95/16.75 x remodel_mult/jak_mult; k_tether = 1.0 tethers the relaxed surface to z_target <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L354-L414>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1603-1751) returns 13 measurements, 5 new in Pass 3 (L1617-1668): coupled-sac dome 53.91 um (ref 54.0), coupled d_HH 19.65 um (ref 19.4), self-consistent p = 0.62 Pa (prediction), maximal fold-locus shift 0.0 across the sweep (ref 0.0), p_half = 372.5 Pa (prediction); the Pass 2 eight remain (dome r = 0.9977, 15-fold r = 0.9953, zone r = 1.0000, Collagenase kappa = 0, specimen s_HH = 0.391, pouch fraction 0.474). Deductions: the zone-curvature r = 1.0000 compares hard-coded 0.0148/0.0151 hinge, 0.0042 notum and -0.0020 x depth fold values (L879-885) with the reference, so it validates nothing (-6); the uniform-growth positional SD discards the 12 solved replicates and appends U(0.18, 0.68) draws (L970) while the WT pinned SD uses the reference SD as its generating sigma (L975) (-5); the uniform-growth fold depths are set equal to their targets (L474-476) instead of measured on the relaxed surface (-3); two of the five new measurements carry `reference_value: None` (L1643, L1663) and the dome / d_HH references are the same prescribed targets as in model-fidelity (-2); the one measurement that is a genuine out-of-sample prediction (p_half) has no published value to test against, which is stated honestly (0)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L474–L476: Uniform-growth d_hn/d_hh/d_hp set equal to the prescribed targets <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L474-L476>",
        "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L879–L885: 7-zone curvature: hinge 0.0148/0.0151, notum 0.0042, fold -0.0020*depth hard-coded; r = 1.0000 is copied <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L879-L885>",
        "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L958–L975: Uniform-growth SD sampled via rng_rep.uniform(0.18, 0.68); WT pinned SD drawn with the reference SD as sigma <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L958-L975>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-measurement-15-point-h-n-h-h-and-h-p-fold-depth-developmental-correlation-64h-96h-ael>,
